  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 759197,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 1000 Miles (Commodore 64) - Synopsis\n\nStep into the roaring world of 1930s Italian motorsport with *1000 Miles* for the Commodore 64! Inspired by the legendary 1000 Miglia rally, this pioneering racing game throws you behind the wheel of a classic car, tackling a grueling, 1000-mile course. While not a realistic simulator, *1000 Miles* was groundbreaking for its time, attempting to simulate car behavior and handling across varied racing conditions – a novel approach in early racing games.\n\nDon't expect pristine audio; the sound quality is rudimentary. Instead, prepare for arcade-style gameplay focused on speed and skillful maneuvering. The game captures the spirit of the historic rally, offering a unique and challenging experience. Though simple by today's standards, *1000 Miles* represents an important early effort in bringing the thrill of classic car racing to home computers, and provides a glimpse into the evolution of racing game design. Relive a piece of gaming history and experience the rush of the 1000 Miglia!"
    },
